{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.LeptonBringSurfaceH33channel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.LeptonBringSurfaceH33channel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.lepton_V_hat_electron_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.lepton_V_hat_electron_formula","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L93-L106","doc":"**THEOREM.** For m = 1 (electron σ_1³), the formula expands as\nV̂_e = W_SYM · q³ + W_STD · ((h² + 1) z + h) + W_ALT · (-q⁻¹)³.\nMatches `mass-endomorphism-tower.md`'s V̂_e ≈ 0.594 paper convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.lepton_V_hat_h3_3channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.lepton_V_hat_h3_3channel","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L78-L91","doc":"The closed-form V̂_ℓ for a lepton with torus braid σ_1^(2m+1),\nusing H_3 3-channel Plancherel formula. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel","label":"prop:lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.hecke_ab_correct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.hecke_ab_correct","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L55-L76","doc":"**THEOREM.** The Hecke recursion produces σ_1^n = a_n σ_1 + b_n\nin H_2(q), given the Hecke quadratic σ_1² = h σ_1 + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.hecke_ab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.hecke_ab","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L45-L53","doc":"The Hecke recursion (a_n, b_n) for σ_1^n in H_2(q):\na_0 = 0, b_0 = 1; (a_{n+1}, b_{n+1}) = (a_n · h + b_n, a_n).\nBy construction: σ_1^n = a_n · σ_1 + b_n in H_2(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.W_STD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.W_STD","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L39-L43","doc":"H_3 Plancherel weight for the standard (2D) irrep λ = (2,1).\nd_q((2,1)) = [2]_q = q + q⁻¹, so W_STD = [2]_q² / [3]_q!. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.W_1D_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LeptonBringSurfaceH3.W_1D_irrep","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/lepton-bring-surface-h3-3channel.lean#L33-L37","doc":"H_3 Plancherel weight for a partition shape (1D irreps).\nFor 1D irreps (sym = (3) or alt = (1,1,1)), d_q(λ) = 1, so the weight\nis `1/[3]_q!` — the `Units` inverse of the q-factorial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}